{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The theorem body was skipped. Use ChoiceBisim as the witnessing bisimulation: matched left-choice transitions follow the assumed bisimilarity, right-choice transitions are identical on both sides, and derivative states are related by ChoiceBisim.bisim.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intro hpq\\n  exists @ChoiceBisim _ _ defs\\n  constructor\\n  · exact ChoiceBisim.choice hpq\\n  intro s1 s2 hr μ'\\n  constructor\\n  · intro s1' htr\\n    cases hr\\n    case choice p q r h =>\\n      cases htr\\n      case choiceL htr =>\\n        obtain ⟨q', htr', hb⟩ := h.follow_fst htr\\n        exact ⟨q', Tr.choiceL htr', ChoiceBisim.bisim hb⟩\\n      case choiceR htr =>\\n        exact ⟨_, Tr.choiceR htr,\\n          ChoiceBisim.bisim (by grind [HomBisimilarity.refl])⟩\\n    case bisim p q h =>\\n      obtain ⟨q', htr', hb⟩ := h.follow_fst htr\\n      exact ⟨q', htr', ChoiceBisim.bisim hb⟩\\n  · intro s2' htr\\n    cases hr\\n    case choice p q r h =>\\n      cases htr\\n      case choiceL htr =>\\n        obtain ⟨p', htr', hb⟩ := h.follow_snd htr\\n        exact ⟨p', Tr.choiceL htr', ChoiceBisim.bisim hb⟩\\n      case choiceR htr =>\\n        exact ⟨_, Tr.choiceR htr,\\n          ChoiceBisim.bisim (by grind [HomBisimilarity.refl])⟩\\n    case bisim p q h =>\\n      obtain ⟨p', htr', hb⟩ := h.follow_snd htr\\n      exact ⟨p', htr', ChoiceBisim.bisim hb⟩\"}"}}
